course: dictionary
lesson: 3935
title: Fsh: a short form and a sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «fsh» is not a real English word you can use on its own. You will meet it in two places: as a short form, and as a sound. Context clues tell you which one you are reading.
explain: FSH is a short form, called an abbreviation. It stands for «follicle-stimulating hormone», a chemical messenger in the body. Doctors and older pupils use the short form in science, so they do not have to write the long name every time.
explain: The other use is a sound. «Fsh! went the can» shows a soft hiss, like air or fizzy drink escaping. Comics and stories often spell sounds like this. Look at the pictures and words around it to know what the sound means.
explain: Check the context. «A fish with no eyes is a fsh» takes away the i, which sounds like "eye", so "fish" becomes "fsh". If the word is in a science text about the body, it is the short form. If it is in a story and sounds like a hiss, it is the sound.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of longer words, often written with capital letters, such as FSH.
fact: FSH stands for «follicle-stimulating hormone», a chemical messenger in the body.
fact: Hormones help grown-up bodies develop and have babies.
fact: «fsh» is not a real English word you can use on its own in a sentence.
fact: Sound spellings like «fsh» or «pssh» show a hiss in comics and stories.
exercise: «Fsh! went the can.» What does fsh show here? | A loud bang, like a door slamming | *A soft hiss, like air escaping | A name for a fish | A quiet giggle
exercise: FSH is an abbreviation. What does FSH stand for? | fish soup with herbs | first state health | a fizzy hiss in a can | *follicle-stimulating hormone
exercise: «A fish with no eyes is a fsh.» Which letter is taken away to turn fish into fsh? | f | *i | s | h
test: In a science book about the body, what does FSH most likely mean? | A school subject | A kind of fish | *A chemical messenger in the body | A loud hiss from a can
test: In phonics, which two sounds blend together to make the sound «fsh»? | sh and i | s and h | f and i | *f and sh
exam: Your friend writes «fsh» in a science report about how bodies change in puberty. What does it most likely stand for? | *follicle-stimulating hormone | A petrol station | A grey, wet day | A fish
